From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NXForge layer <layer@nxforge.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:10:22 +0000
Subject: aspect-ratio: Aspect ratio choice on the Mac (16:9, 16:10, Auto) for
 games with screen-shape stubs

The Mac settings window shows the two screen-shape rows (DM_SCREEN_WIDE, Ocarina of Time; DM_SCREEN_ASPECT, Breath of the Wild and Animal Crossing) as Aspect ratio with 16:9, 16:10 and Auto (match the screen).

DM_SCREEN_WIDE takes shapes from 1.3:1 to 32:9 other than 16:9, so 16x10 renders Ocarina at 2304x1440 with the cameras at 1.6 (upstream #2538 takes only wider than 16:9). DM_SCREEN_ASPECT=auto is resolved on the Mac from the main screen (the iOS front end resolves its own), and left holding the ratio. The main screen's size leaves out a MacBook's notch (safeAreaInsets.top), where a full-screen window does not reach: 3456x2160, 16:10. The window opens in the picture's shape for a taller one too (1152x720).
